# Part 1: init's three roles, before and after

# before
## a. no reviewer has a session yet (no sessions folder, no lock file)
To ask for a review, commit your work on a branch of its own, not on main; you don't need to ask the operator first. Then `handoff post --as implementer --item <item> --to <reviewer> --commit <sha> --title "<title>" --body <file>`, where <reviewer> is reviewer or reviewer-2.
## b. reviewer has a session (Claude Code, a live process); reviewer-2 none
To ask for a review, commit your work on a branch of its own, not on main; you don't need to ask the operator first. Then `handoff post --as implementer --item <item> --to <reviewer> --commit <sha> --title "<title>" --body <file>`, where <reviewer> is reviewer or reviewer-2.
## c. post to reviewer, from an implementer with no binding (HANDOFF_ROLE)
  out: posted #1 request W1 implementer → reviewer: W1 work @ <sha>
  out: # exit 0
## d. post to reviewer-2
  out: posted #2 request W2 implementer → reviewer-2: W2 work @ <sha>
  out: # exit 0
## e. note to the operator
  out: posted #3 note W1 implementer → operator: A question
  out: # exit 0
  err: handoff: told the operator: W1: implementer asks you: A question
## f. reviewer-2 has a session too (Codex, given by command: no host)
To ask for a review, commit your work on a branch of its own, not on main; you don't need to ask the operator first. Then `handoff post --as implementer --item <item> --to <reviewer> --commit <sha> --title "<title>" --body <file>`, where <reviewer> is reviewer or reviewer-2.
## g. reviewer's process has ended; its binding stays
To ask for a review, commit your work on a branch of its own, not on main; you don't need to ask the operator first. Then `handoff post --as implementer --item <item> --to <reviewer> --commit <sha> --title "<title>" --body <file>`, where <reviewer> is reviewer or reviewer-2.
## h. note to reviewer
  out: posted #4 note W1 implementer → reviewer: A note
  out: # exit 0
## i. post to reviewer, a new item
  out: posted #5 request W3 implementer → reviewer: W3 work @ <sha>
  out: # exit 0

# after
## a. no reviewer has a session yet (no sessions folder, no lock file)
To ask for a review, commit your work on a branch of its own, not on main; you don't need to ask the operator first. Then `handoff post --as implementer --item <item> --to <reviewer> --commit <sha> --title "<title>" --body <file>`, where <reviewer> is reviewer or reviewer-2, whichever the operator gives a session; none has one yet.
## b. reviewer has a session (Claude Code, a live process); reviewer-2 none
To ask for a review, commit your work on a branch of its own, not on main; you don't need to ask the operator first. Then `handoff post --as implementer --item <item> --to reviewer --commit <sha> --title "<title>" --body <file>`. reviewer-2 has no session now: send to it only once the operator gives it one.
## c. post to reviewer, from an implementer with no binding (HANDOFF_ROLE)
  out: posted #1 request W1 implementer → reviewer: W1 work @ <sha>
  out: # exit 0
## d. post to reviewer-2
  out: posted #2 request W2 implementer → reviewer-2: W2 work @ <sha>
  out: # exit 0
  err: handoff: no session has reviewer-2 now, so this waits until the operator gives one that role; tell the operator.
## e. note to the operator
  out: posted #3 note W1 implementer → operator: A question
  out: # exit 0
  err: handoff: told the operator: W1: implementer asks you: A question
## f. reviewer-2 has a session too (Codex, given by command: no host)
To ask for a review, commit your work on a branch of its own, not on main; you don't need to ask the operator first. Then `handoff post --as implementer --item <item> --to <reviewer> --commit <sha> --title "<title>" --body <file>`, where <reviewer> is reviewer or reviewer-2.
## g. reviewer's process has ended; its binding stays
To ask for a review, commit your work on a branch of its own, not on main; you don't need to ask the operator first. Then `handoff post --as implementer --item <item> --to reviewer-2 --commit <sha> --title "<title>" --body <file>`. reviewer has no session now: send to it only once the operator gives it one.
## h. note to reviewer
  out: posted #4 note W1 implementer → reviewer: A note
  out: # exit 0
  err: handoff: no session has reviewer now, so this waits until the operator gives one that role; tell the operator.
## i. post to reviewer, a new item
